/**
 * @defgroup locus_tests Unit Tests
 * @brief Unit tests for LOCUS components.
 *
 * LOCUS includes unit tests for all core ELF loader modules.
 * These tests validate defensive behavior, invariants, and
 * failure modes at each abstraction layer.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup elf_image_tests elf_image Tests
 * @ingroup locus_tests
 * @brief Unit tests for the elf_image abstraction.
 *
 * This test suite validates the defensive behavior and core invariants of the
 * elf_image module, including argument validation, file property checks, and
 * safe failure modes.
 *
 * The elf_image module is responsible solely for acquiring and managing a
 * stable, read-only byte view of an ELF file via memory mapping. It performs
 * no ELF semantic validation beyond what is required to establish a valid
 * byte range.
 *
 * These tests intentionally avoid higher-level ELF parsing and interpretation
 * to ensure failures can be attributed exclusively to elf_image behavior.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup elf_ident_tests elf_ident Tests
 * @ingroup locus_tests
 * @brief Unit tests for ELF identification parsing and validation.
 *
 * This test suite validates the defensive behavior of elf_validate_ident(),
 * focusing on argument validation and failure modes at the ELF identification
 * layer.
 *
 * The elf_ident module operates on an already-initialized elf_image_t and
 * interprets only the e_ident[] bytes at the start of the ELF file. These
 * tests intentionally avoid file I/O and higher-level ELF parsing to ensure
 * failures can be attributed solely to ELF identification logic.
 *
 * All test inputs are constructed to respect the elf_image abstraction
 * boundary: elf_ident does not create or manage ELF images, it only consumes
 * them.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup elf_read_tests elf_read Tests
 * @ingroup locus_tests
 * @brief Unit tests for endian-aware ELF field read helpers.
 *
 * This test suite validates the defensive behavior of the elf_read_* helpers,
 * which provide bounds-checked, endian-aware access to multi-byte ELF fields
 * within an ELF image.
 *
 * The elf_read module operates on an already-initialized elf_image_t and
 * validated ELF identification information. These tests focus exclusively on
 * argument validation and failure modes, not on successful decoding paths.
 *
 * Higher-level ELF parsing and semantic validation are intentionally excluded
 * to ensure failures can be attributed solely to elf_read behavior.
 */
